ev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp.skill-go-exec-dev-tcp"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"help":{"markdown":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec](https://pkg.go.dev/os/exec)\n - [https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec](https://pkg.go.dev/syscall#Exec)\n - [https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/](https://semgrep.dev/docs/cheat-sheets/go-command-injection/)\n","text":"Detects execution of network tools commonly used for exfiltration or reverse shells"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-go-exec-network-tools.skill-go-exec-network-tools"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n"},"help":{"markdown":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection)\n","text":"PowerShell Invoke-Expression (IEX) with base64 decoding detected. This pattern\nuses PowerShell's IEX command with base64 decoding to execute obfuscated code.\nThis technique is commonly used for:\n\n- Obfuscated command execution that bypasses basic static analysis\n- Red team exercises and penetration testing\n- Malware delivery and persistence mechanisms\n- Command & Control (C2) payload execution\n\nThe base64 encoding hides the actual commands from security tools and makes\nforensic analysis more difficult. Legitimate use of this pattern is rare.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","id":"skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","name":"skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.command-execution.skill-powershell-iex-base64.skill-powershell-iex-base64"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately."},"help":{"markdown":"Obvious malicious subprocess pattern detected: - Pipe to bash/sh (curl|bash, wget|sh, etc) - Reverse shell tools (nc, netcat, /dev/tcp) - Persistence (crontab, @reboot) HIGH SIGNAL - review immediately.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.command-execution.skill-python-subprocess.skill-python-subprocess-execution)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1059/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/](https://owasp.org/Top10/2025/A05_2025-Injection/)\n - [https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Injection](https://owasp.org/Top10/A03_2021-Inject