-Injection)\n","text":"Hook script contains a bash reverse shell using /dev/tcp or /dev/udp. Scripts in AI\ntool hook directories (.claude/hooks/, .gemini/hooks/, etc.) execute automatically\nwith full user OS permissions on every tool event. Any developer who clones this\nrepository will have an outbound reverse shell opened to an attacker-controlled host\non each session or file operation.\n\nReview the commit history of this file and the hook configuration that invokes it.\n"},"helpUri":"https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell","id":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell","name":"skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')","HIGH CONFIDENCE","OWASP-A01:2017 - Injection","OWASP-A03:2021 - Injection","OWASP-A05:2025 - Injection","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Semgrep Finding: skills.hooks.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell.skill-hook-script-bash-reverse-shell"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Skill uses @reboot cron entry for boot persistence. Detects @reboot cron entries being written to crontab via pipe, which executes commands on every system startup. This is a persistence technique used by attackers to survive reboots."},"help":{"markdown":"Skill uses @reboot cron entry for boot persistence. Detects @reboot cron entries being written to crontab via pipe, which executes commands on every system startup. This is a persistence technique used by attackers to survive reboots.\n\n<b>References:</b>\n - [Semgrep Rule](https://semgrep.dev/r/skills.persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence.skill-cron-reboot-persistence)\n - [https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/003/)